{"name":"Clown Green","hex":"#c4d056","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"clown","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A slapstick performance artist often associated with a circus and usually characterized by bright, oversized clothing, a red nose, face paint, and a brightly colored wig.","A person who acts in a silly fashion."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To act in a silly or playful fashion.","To ridicule, make fun of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/clown"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Clown","blocks":[{"text":"A clown is a person who performs physical comedy and arts in an open-ended fashion, typically while wearing distinct makeup or costuming and reversing folkway-norms. The art of performing as a clown is known as clowning or buffoonery, and the term \"clown\" may be used synonymously with predecessors like jester, joker, buffoon, fool, or harlequin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Auguste_clown_reading_a_book_upside-down.jpg/330px-Auguste_clown_reading_a_book_upside-down.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clown"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Joseph_Grimaldi.jpg/500px-Joseph_Grimaldi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Joseph_Grimaldi.jpg/500px-Joseph_Grimaldi.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Joseph Grimaldi as \"Joey\" the Clown, c. 1810","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoseph_Grimaldi.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/LES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG/500px-LES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/LES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG/500px-LES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Les Rossyann, white clown and clumsy Auguste from France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALES_ROSSYANN_Weisscloun_und_dummer_August.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/G.L._Fox